    <item>
      <title>Declarative State Machines in Orkestra</title>
      <link>http://localhost:8090/blog/declarative-state-machines/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 15 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:8090/blog/declarative-state-machines/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;One of Orkestra&amp;rsquo;s core design principles is that every CRD lifecycle should be an &lt;strong&gt;explicit state machine&lt;/strong&gt; — not implicit logic buried in Go code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In traditional operators, state transitions are encoded in the &lt;code&gt;Reconcile&lt;/code&gt; function. You have to read the code to understand what states exist, what triggers transitions, and what happens on failure. Orkestra makes all of this visible in the Katalog.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;state-machines-in-yaml&#34;&gt;State machines in YAML&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#282a36;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-yaml&#34; data-lang=&#34;yaml&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;spec&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;crds&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;database&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;      &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;operatorBox&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;onCreate&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;          &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;deployments&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            - &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;image&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f1fa8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;postgres:{{ .spec.version }}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;              &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;reconcile&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;          &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;fields&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            - &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;: phase&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;              &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f1fa8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Running&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            - &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;: endpoint&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;              &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ff79c6&#34;&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f1fa8c&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;{{ .metadata.name }}.{{ .metadata.namespace }}.svc&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;onCreate&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;onReconcile&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;onDelete&lt;/code&gt; hooks define the state transitions. The &lt;code&gt;status.fields&lt;/code&gt; declarations define what gets written after each successful transition.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
